  {
   "@id": "http://localhost:8080/seattle-movers-cost/#faq",
   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Ask about a minimum number of hours, travel time to your door, stairs, a long carry from the truck, packing materials, and any bridge toll or ferry fare. On a small job, those extras can make Seattle movers cost far more than the hourly rate suggests. Get every charge listed in the written estimate, which Washington movers must give you for free."
     },
     "name": "What hidden fees show up on a short Seattle move?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Tipping is up to you, and it sits outside what Seattle movers cost on the bill. Moving guides suggest $10.00–$20.00 per mover for a job of up to 4 hours, and $20.00–$65.00 per mover for each full working day. Tip toward the top after a walk-up, a long carry or a day of rain."
     },
     "name": "How much should you tip a Seattle moving crew?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Movers price what you own, not floor area, but as a rough rule of thumb 2,000 square feet is often a 3-bedroom house. A typical local 3-bedroom move costs $1,150–$2,850 at 10 road miles, off peak, with no stairs or extras, with 4 movers at $200–$300 an hour. Seattle movers cost more than that for a house with stairs, a steep driveway or a long carry."
     },
     "name": "What does a 2,000-square-foot Seattle house cost to move?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Usually, yes. The calculator prices any date from October through April as off peak, and crews have more open dates then. Rain slows the work a little, so Seattle movers cost less in winter mainly through lower rates and easier booking, not faster crews. A mid-month weekday is the cheapest slot in any season."
     },
     "name": "Do Seattle movers cost less in winter?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes: the calculator at the top of this page. Enter your ZIP codes, home size, date and stairs, and it shows a price range for your move in about a minute, with no email needed to see it. Use it to judge whether a written estimate of Seattle movers cost sits in a sensible range."
     },
     "name": "Is there a calculator for Seattle movers cost?"
    }
